---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Cta from '../../components/Cta.astro';
const pageSlug = 'compare-hide-it-pro';
const articleLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'Vireault vs Hide it Pro',
  description: 'Compare Vireault with Hide it Pro for hiding and protecting private files on Android.',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Vireault' },
  datePublished: '2026-11-05',
  dateModified: '2026-11-05',
  mainEntityOfPage: 'https://vireault.app/compare/hide-it-pro',
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Vireault vs Hide it Pro"
  description="Vireault vs Hide it Pro: modern local AES-256 vault compared with a veteran Android file-hider app."
  path="/compare/hide-it-pro"
  pageSlug={pageSlug}
  ogType="article"
  jsonLd={articleLd}
  article={{ published: '2026-11-05', modified: '2026-11-05' }}
>
  <div class="container">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ href: '/', label: 'Home' }, { href: '/compare', label: 'Compare' }, { label: 'Hide it Pro' }]} />
    <article class="section prose" style="max-width:none">
      <h1>Vireault vs Hide it Pro</h1>
      <p class="lead">Hide it Pro is one of the best-known Android apps for hiding pictures and files. Vireault focuses on a compact encrypted vault with no account and a clear cryptography stack.</p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Topic</th>
              <th>Vireault</th>
              <th>Hide it Pro (category view)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Primary pitch</td>
              <td>Encrypted local vault</td>
              <td>Hide private data / disguise-oriented privacy utility</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Account</td>
              <td>None</td>
              <td>Typically device-centric; check the current app for any account features</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Encryption described here</td>
              <td>Argon2id + AES-256-GCM + encrypted index</td>
              <td>Consult Hide it Pro’s own documentation for current crypto details</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Media support in Vireault</td>
              <td>Photos, video, audio, PDF import/view</td>
              <td>Broad hider category often covers pictures and files; exact formats vary</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Locking</td>
              <td>PIN / pattern / passphrase, lockout, auto-lock, screenshot blocking</td>
              <td>Passcode-style protection is common in the category</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <Cta pageSlug={pageSlug} heading="Want encryption called out explicitly?" />
      <h2>Choosing between them</h2>
      <p>If you already know Hide it Pro’s interface and it meets your needs, switching is optional. Choose Vireault if you specifically want a no-account vault that documents Argon2id, AES-256-GCM, encrypted backups and optional original deletion after import.</p>
      <h2>Limits to remember</h2>
      <p>Vireault now includes folders, fingerprint unlock on compatible devices, in-app camera capture, and Pro hidden/decoy vaults. It still has no built-in cloud sync. Hide it Pro may include workflows outside that list; verify on Google Play before you decide.</p>
      <p>Continue with <a href="/compare/keepsafe">Keepsafe</a>, <a href="/compare/calculator-vault">calculator vaults</a>, <a href="/features/encryption">encryption</a>, and <a href="/guides/how-to-hide-photos-on-android">how to hide photos on Android</a>.</p>
    </article>
    <Cta pageSlug={pageSlug} />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
